When a neutral charge distribution is considered in the presence of an external electric field, the electric dipole moment arises of its own accord. Expressing
$
  va(E)(va(r)') = ee^((va(r)' - va(r)) dot grad) va(E)(va(r)) = va(E)(va(r)) + ((va(r)' - va(r)) dot grad) va(E) + ((va(r)' - va(r)) dot grad)^2 va(E) + dots.c
$
